;;; some-nice-colors-theme.el --- Dusty maroon and grass on near-black brown -*- lexical-binding: t; -*-

;;; Commentary:

;; A warm, low-glare dark theme.
;;
;; The surfaces are very dark browns that read as black until something
;; warm sits next to them, so the frame recedes and the code does the
;; talking.  Panels -- mode line, popups, code blocks, the current line --
;; are lifted a few points out of that near-black rather than outlined,
;; which keeps the frame quiet at night.
;;
;; The accents are a dusty maroon rose for anything you define (functions,
;; headings, the selection), a dusty grass green for the words the language
;; owns (keywords), and peach, amber, blue, teal and violet for the rest.
;; Every accent is desaturated enough to look at for a full day.
;;
;; Comments are deliberately not whispered: they sit noticeably brighter
;; than the old warm grey and are panelled with their own slightly lifted
;; background, so a comment reads as a small note pinned to the code.
;;
;; The palette below is the whole theme; every colour used anywhere in the
;; face list is named here, and nothing else is hard-coded.  That is what
;; makes `init/some-nice-colors-edit' able to recolour the whole theme live.

;;; Code:

(deftheme some-nice-colors
  "Dusty maroon, grass green and peach on near-black warm browns.")

